-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and check why it was promoted even though the RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16112, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HspU85t38V1SyTfd8i9CT1", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_malformed"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 16112, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HspU85t38V1SyTfd8i9CT1", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19829, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **What went wrong:** checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0 and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it, and find out why it was released. Its test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already failing health checks in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J8NRzKyL47XayE4P4BNgZf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "