t": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **What went wrong:** checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0 and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it, and find out why it was released. Its test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already failing health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}